  "notes": [
   "Parts are unchanged from step 1 (no breadboard; 7 jumper wires: 5 blue signal, 1 red 3.3V, 1 black GND).",
   "The shield is stacked on the Uno; stacking is modelled as joined+electrical edges on the pins the circuit uses (6, 7, 11, 12, 13, 3.3V, GND.1).",
   "Correction to step 1 note: the schematic crosses D7/D6 on purpose. D7 goes to CSB and D6 to DRDY, which matches the text, code and image.",
   "SPI wiring follows the code comment and the Uno's real SPI pins: D13 to SCK, D11 to MOSI, D12 to MISO. The schematic's D12/D11 labels and the image's wire ends are hard to read and look swapped, so I used the electrically correct mapping.",
   "The ground wire goes to the GND header next to 3.3V on the shield's power header (GND.1). The red wire goes to the shield's 3.3V.",
   "The Ethernet cable plugs into the shield's RJ45 socket. Its other end goes to the network, which is not a part in the graph.",
   "SCP1000 and Arduino Ethernet Shield are new part types, since lookup_part found neither."
  ]
 },
